<p>A UN human rights report says Sudan’s Rapid Support Forces (RSF) killed more than 6,000 people over about three days during an assault on the Darfur city of el-Fasher last October. The UN said the attack included widespread atrocities, and that the violence could amount to war crimes and possibly crimes against humanity. The report adds detail to the UN’s wider documentation of abuses in Sudan’s war, and it underscores the danger civilians still face in and around el-Fasher as fighting continues in Darfur.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kXEQ9nYedJ0iq70ny-vNV3ZqIqCtKiDFJ4oaR6O2zHnnwQ6TbkEVF3uDJKmHH90JvWZW-StuTTKBmdXkwQq7IiYiJ9hZc2a_Fs7dssa87r-KSDY9XB94ZH3G9yH4dM7XN1B_3JcHe1rnINYlplaaDZFJgG3q9pjyeUZQeaFF1QwPoGvD14qLByxXFcXK5rw92A' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Report timing: OHCHR released the findings on Friday as part of its human-rights monitoring of Sudan’s conflict.</li><li>Operational framing: The UN report says the October violence unfolded during the RSF’s “final offensive” to capture the besieged city of el-Fasher.</li><li>Characterization: OHCHR called the violence “shocking in its scale and brutality,” language echoed in coverage.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UN Human Rights Office (OHCHR): OHCHR said the RSF’s “final offensive” to capture the besieged city involved alleged abuses that may constitute war crimes and possible crimes against humanity. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202602140225.html'>UN News (via AllAfrica)</a>)</li><li>ABC News / wire report: The report focused on the UN estimate of the death toll over roughly three days during the assault on el-Fasher. (<a href='https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/6000-killed-3-days-rsf-attack-sudans-el-fasher-un-130175430'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.go.com/International/wireStory/6000-killed-3-days-rsf-attack-sudans-el-130175430'>At least 6,000 killed over 3 days during RSF attack on Sudan’s el-Fasher, UN say